sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Platform User
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant Reconciler as MCPServerReconciler<br/>(controller-runtime)
    participant MCPPod as MCP Server Pod<br/>User-defined port

    Note over User,MCPPod: Flow 1: MCPServer Reconciliation

    User->>K8sAPI: Create MCPServer CR<br/>(mcp.x-k8s.io/v1alpha1)
    K8sAPI->>Reconciler: Watch event<br/>ServiceAccount token auth
    Reconciler->>Reconciler: Validate MCPServer spec
    Reconciler->>K8sAPI: Create/Update Deployment<br/>HTTPS/6443, SA token
    Reconciler->>K8sAPI: Create/Update Service<br/>HTTPS/6443, SA token
    Reconciler->>K8sAPI: Create/Update NetworkPolicy<br/>HTTPS/6443, SA token

    Note over Reconciler,MCPPod: MCP Handshake (exponential backoff 10s-2min, max 10 retries)

    Reconciler->>MCPPod: MCP Initialize handshake<br/>StreamableHTTP<br/>HTTP or HTTPS (configurable TLS)
    MCPPod-->>Reconciler: Server identity + capabilities<br/>(tools, resources, prompts, logging, completions)
    Note right of MCPPod: HTTP 401/403 treated as reachable

    Reconciler->>K8sAPI: Update MCPServer status via SSA<br/>HTTPS/6443, SA token

    Note over User,MCPPod: Flow 2: Config Change Detection

    K8sAPI->>Reconciler: ConfigMap/Secret watch event<br/>metadata change detected
    Reconciler->>K8sAPI: Get ConfigMap/Secret data<br/>HTTPS/6443, SA token
    Reconciler->>Reconciler: Compute config hash (SHA-256)
    Reconciler->>K8sAPI: Update Deployment pod template annotation<br/>with new config hash (triggers rolling update)

    Note over User,MCPPod: Flow 3: Metrics Collection

    participant Prom as Prometheus
    Prom->>Reconciler: GET /metrics<br/>HTTPS/8443<br/>TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview
    Reconciler-->>Prom: Prometheus metrics<br/>(condition_info, failure counters, phase durations)
